<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proelĭor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prael-</span></b> ), ātus, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i>
			[proelium], <i>to join battle</i>, <i>to
				engage in battle</i>, <i>fight</i> (class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legiones in ipsis fluminis ripis proeliabantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 2, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad Syracusas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 25, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ita proelians interficitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 2, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fortissime proeliando,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. G. 8, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apes inter se et cum alteris quasi cum exteris
					gentibus proeliantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					9, 9, 5</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. Alex. 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				1, 78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 2, 11, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bella Domini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					1 Reg. 18, 17</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In mal. part.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex animo proeliabor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 119, 21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			gen., <i>to contend</i>,
			<i>fight with words</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vehementer proeliatus sum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 1, 16, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
